  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A single-slit is illuminated using monochromatic red light, a diffraction pattern is formed on a screen behind the slit and the width of the central maximum is measured to be <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{r}\"></span>. When the colour of the light is changed to violet the width of the central maximum is measured to be <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{v}\"></span>, and when the colour of the light is changed to yellow the width of the central maximum is measured to be <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{y}\"></span>. What is the correct relationship between <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{r}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{v}\"></span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{y}\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{r}&lt;x_{y}&lt;x_{v}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{v}&lt;x_{y}&lt;x_{r}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{y}&lt;x_{r}&lt;x_{v}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{v}&lt;x_{r}&lt;x_{y}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
